// Title: PUA - RunXCmd Execution
// Sigma ID: 93199800-b52a-4dec-b762-75212c196542
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-01-24 | Modified: 2023-02-14
// ATT&CK: execution, T1569.002, S0029
// Description: Detects the use of the RunXCmd tool to execute commands with System or TrustedInstaller accounts
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use by administrators
// References:
//   - https://www.d7xtech.com/free-software/runx/
//   - https://www.winhelponline.com/blog/run-program-as-system-localsystem-account-windows/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pua_runxcmd.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains " /account=system " or ProcessCommandLine contains " /account=ti ") and ProcessCommandLine contains "/exec="
